# The loader's 1:1 map is gone once the kernel loads its own tables: a
# ring-0 read of virtual 0x200000, which the loader mapped 1:1 and which is
# RAM, faults, and the fault report names that address in CR2.
#
# This needs the kernel's exception reporting. Without it the #PF finds the
# firmware's IDT, which the kernel's tables no longer map, and QEMU reports a
# triple fault as a shutdown, so the scenario fails.
cmdline: test=lowmem
exit: failure
expect: microL4 kernel
expect: paging: kernel PML4 at
expect: lowmem: physical 0x200000 reads
expect: lowmem: reading virtual 0x200000
expect: KERNEL PANIC
expect: 200000
